# Sotto self-host: the Railway service variables, and nothing else.
#
# The supported install is tools/setup_selfhost_railway.py (docs/AGENT-ONBOARDING.md). It sets
# exactly the two variables below on the service it creates and refuses a service carrying any
# other non-RAILWAY_* variable. You do not write either value by hand: your inputs (Railway
# project/environment, owner phone, Photon line and project, Gemini key, timezone, and optional
# background_unmetered boolean (default false, explicit uncapped background spending opt-in)) go in the
# helper's protected mode-0600 JSON config instead.
#
# The supervised image never forwards ambient variables: the bootstrap clears its environment and
# the supervisor builds the receiver's and Node's environments from the launch envelope alone. The
# SOTTO_SETUP_LOG_FD is an internal one-use descriptor for the private setup-link boot line only;
# do not supply it. Ordinary receiver and Node output remain suppressed.
# The variables it injects, the ones a receiver run sets for its child, and the settings that keep
# their code defaults are all listed in RAILWAY.md § Environment variables, marked "do not set"
# or "fixed". SOTTO_SKILL_COMPOSITION_PROOF is receiver-owned child proof, including meeting-prep;
# never supply it as a service variable.

# The private launch envelope (manifest, generated runtime/Bridge/control tokens, Photon and
# Gemini credentials, timezone), bound to this service, /data volume, domain and setup marker.
# Written by the setup helper; read by adapters/sotto/selfhost_bootstrap.py.
SOTTO_SELFHOST_LAUNCH=<written by tools/setup_selfhost_railway.py>

# The helper's ownership marker; the bootstrap requires it to match the envelope.
SOTTO_SETUP_REQUEST=<written by tools/setup_selfhost_railway.py>

# Sotto Cloud tenants only (never on a self-host): the managed launch envelope, written by Sotto's
# own tenant provisioning and read by adapters/sotto/managed_bootstrap.py.
# SOTTO_MANAGED_LAUNCH=<written by Sotto Cloud provisioning>

# Railway injects PORT (must be 8080), RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN and the RAILWAY_*_ID values the
# bootstrap checks against the envelope; do not set them. Leave RAILWAY_DEPLOYMENT_DRAINING_SECONDS
# unset (RAILWAY.md).
